course: dictionary
lesson: 7813
title: Quicken: speeding up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Quicken means to become faster, or to make something faster. «Fear makes the heart beat faster, breathing quicken and muscles get ready to move.» When you are scared, your body speeds up, so quicken fits the idea of getting faster.
explain: Look at the words around it. A faster heartbeat and quicker breathing show that quicken means speed up. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "breathing speed up and muscles get ready to move" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Quicken can also mean to become more lively or active. «Her heart quickened» means her heart beat faster. «He quickened his pace» means he walked or ran faster. To quicken your pace means to hurry.
fact: Quicken is a verb, so it can change to quickens, quickened or quickening.
fact: «Quicken» means to become faster or to make something faster.
fact: «Quickened» is the past tense: «My pulse quickened» means my heartbeat got faster.
fact: Quicken the process means to make a task or job happen sooner.
fact: Your heartbeat quickens during exercise or when you are scared.
exercise: «He quickened his pace when the rain started.» What does quickened mean here? | Sang loudly | Turned around slowly | Stopped completely | * Went faster
exercise: Which phrase means to walk or run faster? | Lose your way | Count to ten | * Quicken your pace | Hold your breath
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means speeds up: «Fear makes the heart beat faster, breathing quicken and muscles get ready to move.» | ready | * quicken | move | muscles
test: Why does your heart quicken when you are scared? | Your heart is full of sleep | It is too cold outside | Your heart stops for a while | * Your body gets ready to run or move fast
test: «My pulse quickened.» What does this tell you? | * My heartbeat got faster | My pulse became very quiet | I felt sleepy | My pulse stopped
exam: «The teacher asked us to quicken the process, so we finished the task sooner.» What does quicken the process mean? | Stop the process for good | Forget the process | Make the process longer | * Make the process happen faster
